WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.338
(light ambient music)
- It's a great life.

00:00:04.338 --> 00:00:07.171
I wouldn't change it for anything.

00:00:09.732 --> 00:00:10.899
I was a model.

00:00:13.393 --> 00:00:16.384
I was always in heels and
pumps and platform shoes,

00:00:16.384 --> 00:00:20.001
and I worried about my
weight. There just came a time

00:00:20.001 --> 00:00:24.353
I just said, “Enough,
I'm not happy anymore.”

00:00:24.353 --> 00:00:27.826
I came to Alaska with one dog
and about $500 in my pocket

00:00:27.826 --> 00:00:31.003
'cause I wanted to be a sled-dog musher.

00:00:31.003 --> 00:00:34.984
(light piano music)
I knew that life

00:00:34.984 --> 00:00:37.369
in Alaska was for me basically the moment

00:00:37.369 --> 00:00:39.619
I stepped off the airplane.

00:00:40.641 --> 00:00:44.048
I got here and the
mountains just blew me away.

00:00:44.048 --> 00:00:48.031
It's like how some people
feel when they see the ocean.

00:00:48.031 --> 00:00:50.383
I personally don't feel
isolated at all in Alaska

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:53.580
because I'm surrounded by a lot
of dogs and a lot of family.

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:56.247
Racing is fun, and I enjoy that.

00:00:57.109 --> 00:01:01.049
But there is a great need
for rescue in Alaska.

00:01:01.049 --> 00:01:02.799
We take dogs that are rejected

00:01:02.799 --> 00:01:05.032
from other teams and other kennels.

00:01:05.032 --> 00:01:07.543
They all have their own unique stories,

00:01:07.543 --> 00:01:11.710
and this is, to me, the most
rewarding work we can do.

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:18.523
I'm training for the Iditarod 2016.

00:01:18.523 --> 00:01:20.334
The Iditarod is the world's longest

00:01:20.334 --> 00:01:24.436
and probably most well
known sled dog race.

00:01:24.436 --> 00:01:26.629
It's a thousand miles, starts in Anchorage

00:01:26.629 --> 00:01:29.398
and goes to Nome, and it
covers some amazing country

00:01:29.398 --> 00:01:33.565
and it goes up on the coast
off of the Bering Sea.

00:01:38.201 --> 00:01:41.413
To be on the sled with
the dogs feels amazing.

00:01:41.413 --> 00:01:43.617
You're part of this wild
world where there's caribou

00:01:43.617 --> 00:01:45.430
and there's moose, and
you got the sunrise,

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:47.466
you got the sunset, you
got the stars over you,

00:01:47.466 --> 00:01:49.714
you got the moon over you.

00:01:49.714 --> 00:01:53.631
And it's a great feeling
to be a part of that.

